    "name":  "Toxic liver disease with chronic active hepatitis with ascites",
    "module":  "hepatobiliary",
    "category":  "disease",
    "description":  "Toxic liver disease with chronic active hepatitis progressing to ascites indicates that drug-induced hepatic injury has caused sufficient portal hypertension and reduced synthetic function to result in peritoneal fluid accumulation. This represents advanced DILI with features of decompensated liver disease. At this stage the offending agent should have already been withdrawn; persistence of disease suggests either ongoing exposure, or progression to an autoimmune phenotype that requires immunosuppressive therapy (corticosteroids, azathioprine). Liver transplantation may be required in refractory cases.",
